  "name": "Monaco Editor language detection from file extension",
  "pinned": false,
  "description": "Here's a 5-line summary:\n\n1. **`Editor.vue`** was updated to accept a new `fileName` prop alongside the existing `language` prop for auto-detecting Monaco language.\n2. A **`EXTENSION_LANGUAGE_MAP`** constant was added mapping 60+ file extensions (`.js`, `.py`, `.rs`, etc.) to their Monaco language identifiers.\n3. A **`resolvedLanguage`** computed property was introduced, prioritizing the explicit `language` prop, then falling back to extension detection from `fileName`, then defaulting to `'plaintext'`.\n4. **`CodeViewer.vue`** was updated to pass `:fileName=\"file\"` to all `<Editor>` instances instead of `:language=\"fileLanguage\"`, delegating language resolution to the editor.\n5. The `fileLanguage` computed in `CodeViewer.vue` was **preserved** solely for `VueCodeHighlighter`, which still requires `hljs`-compatible language names.",
